{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019fHue9Etp42MU6QedNqmZw","type":"tool_result","content":"107\tpub fn prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu<HS, TS>(\n108\t    transcript: &mut TS,\n109\t    mpk: &DeviceMultiStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n110\t    ctx: &ProvingContext<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n111\t    save_memory: bool,\n112\t    monomial_num_y_threshold: u32,\n113\t    sm_count: u32,\n114\t) -> Result<(GkrProof<HS::SC>, BatchConstraintProof<HS::SC>, Vec<EF>), LogupZerocheckError>\n115\twhere\n116\t    HS: GpuHashScheme,\n117\t    TS: GpuFiatShamirTranscript<HS::SC>,\n118\t{\n119\t    let logup_gkr_span = info_span!(\"prover.rap_constraints.logup_gkr\", phase = \"prover\").entered();\n120\t    let l_skip = mpk.params.l_skip;\n121\t    let constraint_degree = mpk.max_constraint_degree;\n122\t    let num_traces = ctx.per_trace.len();\n123\t\n124\t    // Traces are sorted\n125\t    let n_max = log2_strict_usize(ctx.per_trace[0].1.common_main.height()).saturating_sub(l_skip);\n126\t    // Gather interactions metadata, including interactions stacked layout which depends on trace\n127\t    // heights\n128\t    let mut total_interactions = 0u64;\n129\t    let interactions_meta: Vec<_> = ctx\n130\t        .per_trace\n131\t        .iter()\n132\t        .map(|(air_idx, air_ctx)| {\n133\t            let pk = &mpk.per_air[*air_idx];\n134\t\n135\t            let num_interactions = pk.vk.symbolic_constraints.interactions.len();\n136\t            let height = air_ctx.common_main.height();\n137\t            let log_height = log2_strict_usize(height);\n138\t            let log_lifted_height = log_height.max(l_skip);\n139\t            total_interactions += (num_interactions as u64) << log_lifted_height;\n140\t            (num_interactions, log_lifted_height)\n141\t        })\n142\t        .collect();\n143\t    // Implicitly, the width of this stacking should be 1\n144\t    let n_logup = calculate_n_logup(l_skip, total_interactions);\n145\t    // There's no stride threshold for `interactions_layout` because there's no univariate skip for\n146\t    // GKR\n147\t    let interactions_layout = StackedLayout::new(0, l_skip + n_logup, interactions_meta).unwrap();\n148\t\n149\t    // Grind to increase soundness of random sampling for LogUp\n150\t    let logup_pow_witness = transcript\n151\t        .grind_gpu(mpk.params.logup.pow_bits)\n152\t        .map_err(LogupZerocheckError::Grind)?;\n153\t    let alpha_logup = transcript.sample_ext();\n154\t    let beta_logup = transcript.sample_ext();\n155\t    debug!(%alpha_logup, %beta_logup);\n156\t\n157\t    let has_interactions = !interactions_layout.sorted_cols.is_empty();\n158\t    let mut prover = LogupZerocheckGpu::new(\n159\t        mpk,\n160\t        ctx,\n161\t        n_logup,\n162\t        interactions_layout,\n163\t        alpha_logup,\n164\t        beta_logup,\n165\t        save_memory,\n166\t        monomial_num_y_threshold,\n167\t        sm_count,\n168\t    )?;\n169\t    let n_global = prover.n_global;\n170\t\n171\t    let total_leaves = 1 << (l_skip + n_logup);\n172\t    prover\n173\t        .mem\n174\t        .emit_metrics_with_label(\"prover.before_gkr_input_evals\");\n175\t    prover.mem.reset_peak();\n176\t    let (inputs, alpha) = if has_interactions {\n177\t        log_gkr_input_evals(\n178\t            &prover.trace_interactions,\n179\t            mpk,\n180\t            ctx,\n181\t            l_skip,\n182\t            alpha_logup,\n183\t            &prover.d_challenges,\n184\t            total_leaves,\n185\t        )?\n186\t    } else {\n187\t        (DeviceBuffer::new(), EF::ZERO)\n188\t    };\n189\t    // Set memory limit for batch MLE based on inputs buffer size\n190\t    prover.gkr_mem_contribution = inputs.len() * std::mem::size_of::<Frac<EF>>();\n191\t    prover.memory_limit_bytes = prover.gkr_mem_contribution;\n192\t    if !prover.save_memory {\n193\t        const DEFAULT_MEMORY_LIMIT: usize = 5 << 30; // 5GiB\n194\t        if prover.memory_limit_bytes > DEFAULT_MEMORY_LIMIT {\n195\t            tracing::warn!(\n196\t                \"prover.memory_limit_bytes {} already exceeds 5GiB\",\n197\t                prover.memory_limit_bytes\n198\t            );\n199\t        }\n200\t        prover.memory_limit_bytes = DEFAULT_MEMORY_LIMIT;\n201\t    }\n202\t    prover.mem.emit_metrics_with_label(\"prover.gkr_input_evals\");\n203\t\n204\t    let (frac_sum_proof, mut xi) =\n205\t        fractional_sumcheck_gpu(transcript, inputs, alpha, true, &mut prover.mem)?;\n206\t    while xi.len() != l_skip + n_global {"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KqFCVJDc9WJFhZ42umbk3D","session_id":"f1ad9314-c536-427a-92c1-585cbcf5d248","uuid":"92631ff9-6a06-46e3-b7b3-072031db0bff","timestamp":"2026-04-12T19:59:47.569Z"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a70ed3a57f100cfeb","tool_use_id":"toolu_01JJGkZvpHnrD7Kst4EdxFiK","status":"completed","output_file":"","summary":"Research Round 0 code path","usage":{"total_tokens":53750,"tool_uses":46,"duration_ms":85412},"uuid":"dd6e4996-631b-4829-bd3b-6977a5006479","session_id":"f1ad9314-c536-427a-92c1-585cbcf5d248"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JJGkZvpHnrD7Kst4EdxFiK","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive final report.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've thoroughly traced the Round 0 constraint evaluation code path in the CUDA GPU prover. Here's the complete analysis:\n\n### **Entry Point & Main Loop**\n\n**File**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\n**Entry Function**: `fn sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` (line 598-884)\n- Called from line 224 in the same file during proof generation\n- Processes all AIR instances sequentially in a single loop (line 732-880)\n\n### **The Per-AIR Loop Structure (Lines 732-880)**\n\nThe loop iterates through each of the 623 AIRs with these key steps per AIR:\n\n1. **Metadata Setup** (lines 744-772):\n   - Clone symbolic constraints from proving key (line 745)\n   - Extract constraint degree, compute generator roots, gather trace pointers\n   - Allocate and upload main trace pointers vector to GPU: `d_main_parts = main_parts.to_device()` (line 768)\n\n2. **GPU Constraint Evaluation** (lines 777-790):\n   - Call `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` → kernel `_zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints`\n   - Allocates intermediates and temp_sums buffers on GPU\n   - Returns evaluated sum buffer (device-side)\n\n3. **CPU Post-Processing for Zerocheck** (lines 791-827):\n   - **D2H copy**: `q_evals = sum_buffer.to_host()` (line 792) — GPU synchronization point\n   - **Transpose**: Rearrange `q_evals` from row-major cosets to column-major (lines 795-801)\n   - **iDFT**: `UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft()` (line 802) — CPU serial iDFT\n   - **Polynomial construction**: Compute coefficients via Lagrange basis interpolation (lines 810-818)\n\n4. **GPU Interaction Evaluation** (lines 831-846):\n   - **Per-AIR CPU work**: Build symbolic DAG for interactions (lines 162-180 in `round0.rs`)\n     - `SymbolicDagBuilder::new()` (line 162)\n     - `dag_builder.add_expr()` for each interaction count/message (lines 165-172)\n     - `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()` DAG compilation (line 181)\n     - Build weight vectors: `numer_weights`, `denom_weights` (lines 182-203)\n     - GPU upload: `d_numer_weights = numer_weights.to_device()`, `d_denom_weights = denom_weights.to_device()`, `d_rules = encoded_rules.to_device()` (lines 204-210)\n   - Call `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` → kernel `_logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0`\n\n5. **CPU Post-Processing for Logup** (lines 847-879):\n   - **D2H copy**: `evals = sum.to_host()` (line 848) — GPU synchronization point\n   - **Fraction unpacking**: Split evals into numerator/denominator (line 850)\n   - **Transpose**: Two rearrangements for row-major cosets (lines 858-867)\n   - **iDFT × 2**: `UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft()` twice for numer/denom (lines 869-878)\n\n### **Identified Per-AIR Overhead**\n\n#### **GPU-side bottleneck (per AIR):**\n- Two kernel launches: `_zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` + `_logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0`\n- **Two GPU synchronization points**: `to_host()` calls (lines 792, 848)\n  - These are the main CPU stalls — each blocks until GPU kernels complete\n  - With 623 AIRs → ~1,246 sync points\n\n#### **CPU-side bottleneck (per AIR) — THE DOMINANT ISSUE:**\n1. **Interaction DAG construction** (lines 162-180 in round0.rs):\n   - `SymbolicDagBuilder` allocation and node addition (varies with # interactions)\n   - DAG → rules compilation (`SymbolicRulesGpu::new`)\n   - Weight vector computation loop\n   - **Scales per AIR**: Not with total cells/constraints\n\n2. **Data transposition**:\n   - Two transpose operations: lines 795-801 (zerocheck), 858-867 (logup numer+denom)\n   - O(num_cosets × skip_domain) per operation = O(constraint_degree × 2^l_skip)\n   - **Scales per AIR despite parallelizable work**\n\n3. **Inverse DFT (iDFT)**:\n   - `from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft()` (lines 802, 869, 874):\n     - `idft_batch()` call (line 640 in `prover/poly.rs`)\n     - Lagrange basis interpolation (lines 644-681)\n     - CPU serial FFT + coefficient unshifting\n   - **Three iDFT calls per AIR** (one for zerocheck, two for logup)\n   - **Serial CPU operation** — can't be parallelized across AIRs without batching\n\n4. **Temporary buffer allocations**:\n   - Lines 715, 768: `to_device()` calls for selector columns and main trace pointers\n   - Lines 668, 611: λ-pows, eq_3b uploads per-AIR\n   - Using `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` but still adds per-AIR overhead\n\n#### **Pre-loop global allocations (amortized)**:\n- Lines 610-614: λ powers (once for all AIRs)\n- Lines 617-623: λ combinations for AIRs with monomials (per AIR with monomials)\n- Lines 628-671: eq_3b weights for interactions (per AIR with interactions)\n- Lines 705-718: Selector base matrices (per AIR)\n\n### **Why Performance Scales with AIR Count Despite Constant Total Work**\n\nFrom the profiling report (lines 73-82), the bottleneck is **CPU post-processing overhead that doesn't scale with data volume**:\n\n1. **DAG compilation per-AIR**: Even small AIRs (height 8-64) require full DAG construction\n2. **iDFT per-AIR**: Three separate iDFT calls, each ~5-15% overhead for small sizes\n3. **Transpose overhead**: O(constraint_degree) work regardless of AIR size\n4. **GPU sync stalls**: 1,246 sync points = ~1ms per AIR even with instant kernels\n\nWith 623 AIRs at APC 300 vs 99 AIRs:\n- Total GPU work: ~2x less (same cells, same constraints)\n- Per-AIR CPU overhead: ~6.3x more (623 iterations vs 99)\n- Result: 662ms (99 AIRs) → Net time increases despite lower total work\n\n### **Key Files & Line Numbers**\n\n| Component | File | Line(s) | Function |\n|-----------|------|---------|----------|\n| Main loop | `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` | 732-880 | Per-AIR iteration |\n| Constraint eval | `logup_zerocheck/round0.rs` | 31-124 | `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` |\n| Interaction eval | `logup_zerocheck/round0.rs` | 132-275 | `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` + DAG build (161-207) |\n| Zerocheck post-proc | `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` | 791-827 | Transpose + iDFT for constraints |\n| Logup post-proc | `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` | 847-879 | Transpose + iDFT for interactions |\n| iDFT implementation | `stark-backend/src/prover/poly.rs` | 621-683 | `from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft()` |\n| GPU FFI definitions | `cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` | 328-350, 288-309, 924-967, 977-1020 | Kernel declarations & wrappers |\n| Interaction monomial prep | `logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs` | 509-580 | `compute_logup_combinations()` |\n| Lambda monomial prep | `logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs` | 79-100 | `compute_lambda_combinations()` |\n\n### **Optimization Insights from Prior Work**\n\nThe previous attempt to pipeline kernel launches (eliminating per-AIR GPU sync) achieved only **3% improvement** at APC 300 (report lines 46). This confirms:\n- GPU kernel launches complete almost instantly (tiny sum buffers copy back immediately)\n- **The real bottleneck is CPU post-processing** (transpose, iDFT, DAG compilation) — not GPU stall time\n- **Per-AIR overhead doesn't scale with data**: 623 small AIRs spend most time in CPU serialization, not GPU work\n\nThe solution would require CPU-GPU overlap strategies (double-buffering batches) or kernel fusion (combining small AIRs into single GPU kernel) rather than sync pipelining."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1ad9314-c536-427a-92c1-585cbcf5d248","uuid":"38034731-a050-4e6a-8220-f8a2d6ca45c6","timestamp":"2026-04-12T19:59:50.915Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the Round 0 constraint evaluation code path in the CUDA GPU prover for a STARK proof system. The codebase is at /home/georg/stark-backend.\n\nKey facts:\n- Round 0 takes 177ms with 99 AIR instances but 662ms with 623 AIR instances, despite the total work (cells, constraints) being 2x