.width(),\n                l_skip,\n            )\n        }\n    }\n    self.q_evals.push(folded_evals);\n}\n```\n- **Per-commit** (not directly per-AIR, but one loop per commit which may be 1 + num_AIRs)\n- **Per-trace**: One kernel launch per trace within each commit\n\n**fold_mle_evals** (Between subsequent rounds): (stacked_reduction.rs:918-948)\n```rust\nlet (folded_q_evals, input_ptrs, output_ptrs): (Vec<_>, Vec<_>, Vec<_>) = self\n    .q_evals  // All commits' evaluations\n    .iter()\n    .map(|q| {\n        let folded = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(q.len() >> 1);\n        (folded, q.as_ptr(), output_ptr)\n    })\n    .multiunzip();\n\nunsafe {\n    fold_mle(\n        &self.d_input_ptrs,\n        &self.d_output_ptrs,\n        &self.d_q_widths,\n        self.q_evals.len(),  // Number of commits\n        ...\n    )\n}\n```\n- **Per-commit**: Batch kernel launch for all commits at once\n- **Work**: Folding MLEs from height `2^k` to `2^(k-1)`\n\n### 5. **Why Does Stacked Reduction Scale Inversely with AIR Count?**\n\nThis is the crucial insight:\n\n**The Problem**: More AIRs → **smaller traces per AIR** on average (fixed total work distributed across more AIRs)\n\n**Why Timing Increases**:\n\n1. **Per-AIR Overhead**: \n   - Each AIR triggers its own GPU kernel launch (expensive: context switch, memory setup, synchronization)\n   - Round 0: N kernel launches (one per AIR)\n   - Rounds 1..n_stack: N kernel launches per round × n_stack rounds = N × n_stack launches total\n   - With 99 AIRs: 99 + 99×n_stack launches\n   - With 623 AIRs: 623 + 623×n_stack launches\n\n2. **D2H Copy Overhead**:\n   - Each AIR needs its own `d_accum` buffer copied back to host (stacked_reduction.rs:904)\n   - Round 0: CPU reconstruction (1 operation)\n   - Rounds 1..n_stack: N D2H copies per round\n   - With 99 AIRs: 1 + 99×n_stack copies\n   - With 623 AIRs: 1 + 623×n_stack copies\n\n3. **Window Processing Overhead**:\n   - The loop at line 833 (`for window in self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2)`) executes once per AIR\n   - With 99 AIRs: 99 iterations per round\n   - With 623 AIRs: 623 iterations per round\n   - Each iteration fills buffers, launches kernels, retrieves results\n\n4. **Reduced Per-Kernel Efficiency**:\n   - **Scenario 114 AIRs (99 actual + common)**: \n     - If 99 AIRs uniformly distributed, each has ~2x more columns on average\n     - Each kernel: larger work per launch, better GPU utilization\n     - Fewer launches, less overhead\n   \n   - **Scenario 624 AIRs (623 actual + common)**:\n     - Each AIR has ~0.33x the columns on average\n     - Each kernel: smaller work per launch, underutilized GPU\n     - More launches, more overhead\n     - More synchronization points\n\n5. **Shared Buffer Reuse**:\n   - `d_accum` (line 844-846 in batch_sumcheck_poly_eval): `fill_zero()` for each AIR\n   - `d_block_sums` (line 532-534 in batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly): `resize()` as needed per AIR\n   - More AIRs = more memory management operations\n\n### 6. **Key Per-AIR Processing Differences**\n\n| Operation | Per-AIR | Files | Frequency |\n|-----------|---------|-------|-----------|\n| Kernel Launch (Round 0) | Yes | stacked_reduction.rs:540 | Once per AIR |\n| Kernel Launch (Rounds 1..n_stack) | Yes | stacked_reduction.rs:864/887 | N times per round |\n| D2H Copy (Rounds 1..n_stack) | Yes | stacked_reduction.rs:904 | N times per round |\n| Buffer Zeroing (Rounds 1..n_stack) | Yes | stacked_reduction.rs:844 | N times per round |\n| fold_ple | Per-commit | stacked_reduction.rs:717 | Once per AIR (mostly) |\n| fold_mle | Per-commit (batched) | stacked_reduction.rs:937 | Once across all AIRs |\n\n### 7. **Files and Key Line Numbers Summary**\n\n| Component | File | Lines | Description |\n|-----------|------|-------|-------------|\n| Main GPU function | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | 185-270 | Entry point `prove_stacked_opening_reduction_gpu` |\n| Struct definition | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | 52-110 | `StackedReductionGpu` with per-AIR trace pointers |\n| Initialization (per-AIR loop) | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | 305-317 | Building `stacked_per_commit` from AIRs |\n| Window metadata | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | 353-377 | Creating `ht_diff_idxs` for per-AIR processing |\n| Round 0: Per-AIR kernels | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | 508-552 | Loop over traces, launch kernel per AIR |\n| Round 0: CPU reconstruction | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | 554-644 | NTT-based polynomial multiplication |\n| Round k: Per-AIR kernels | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | 833-911 | Loop over windows, per-AIR processing |\n| Round k: Degenerate kernel | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | 848-878 | For AIRs with striding |\n| Round k: Normal kernel | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | 880-901 | For standard AIRs |\n| fold_ple_evals | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | 706-748 | Per-commit trace folding |\n| fold_mle_evals | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | 918-948 | Batched MLE folding |\n| CUDA wrapper functions | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs` | 102-273 | Safe wrapper around FFI kernels |\n| Layout definition | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/prover/stacked_pcs.rs` | 18-76 | `StackedLayout` and `StackedSlice` |\n| Config | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/config.rs` | 54-149 | `SystemParams` with `l_skip`, `n_stack` |\n| Device struct | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/device.rs` | 9-43 | `GpuDevice` with system config |\n\n### 8. **Root Cause of Inverse Scaling**\n\nThe scaling behavior (114ms for 99 AIRs vs 318ms for 623 AIRs despite 2x less total work) is dominated by:\n\n1. **GPU Kernel Launch Overhead** (superlinear in AIR count):\n   - Fixed cost per launch (~microseconds) × number of launches\n   - Number of launches ∝ AIR count × n_stack\n\n2. **Host-Device Communication Overhead**:\n   - D2H memcpy for `d_accum` (line 904) × N AIRs × n_stack rounds\n   - Buffer allocation/deallocation per AIR\n\n3. **CPU-Side Loop Overhead**:\n   - Loop iterations (line 833) × N AIRs × n_stack rounds\n   - Each iteration: set up pointers, check conditions, reduce results\n\n4. **Reduced GPU Occupancy**:\n   - With 623 AIRs sharing fixed SM count, each kernel gets fewer threads\n   - Underutilized warps = wasted compute\n\nThe batched `fold_mle` (line 937) is efficient, but the per-AIR `sumcheck_poly_eval` is not—it's fundamentally a loop-based design that doesn't scale well to many AIRs."}],"totalDurationMs":94124,"totalTokens":56268,"totalToolUseCount":31,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":908,"cache_read_input_tokens":49861,"output_tokens":5497,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":908},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5497,"cache_read_input_tokens":49861,"cache_creation_input_tokens":908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":908,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":18,"searchCount":1,"bashCount":12,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
