{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01NcxKJ4EChFs4wCe4FZWd3w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VyRsyQhYFKZpLYPRKkEjSV","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-12-2245-parallelize-round0-cpu-postprocess\n\nRound 0 constraint evaluation at APC 300 spends ~200ms of its 662ms total on serial CPU post-processing (transpose + iDFT + polynomial construction), executed once per AIR × 3 calls inside a sequential loop over 623 AIRs. This work is embarrassingly parallel — each AIR's post-processing is independent. Restructuring the loop to collect raw GPU results first, then batch-process them with rayon's `par_iter` across 32 cores, should reduce this CPU overhead from ~200ms to ~7-13ms, yielding an estimated 28% improvement on Round 0 and 7-8% on STARK excl trace.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":980,"cache_read_input_tokens":96566,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":980},"output_tokens":65,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1ad9314-c536-427a-92c1-585cbcf5d248","uuid":"984b72ed-c6be-4fb1-af02-457f3a47b34c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VyRsyQhYFKZpLYPRKkEjSV","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1ad9314-c536-427a-92c1-585cbcf5d248","uuid":"8198b063-3712-436f-aa9f-5818d6b29c3c","timestamp":"2026-04-12T20:06:08.579Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-12-2245-parallelize-round0-cpu-postprocess\n\nRound 0 constraint evaluation at APC 300 spends ~200ms of its 662ms total on serial CPU post-processing (transpose + iDFT + polynomial construction), executed once per AIR × 3 calls inside a sequential loop over 623 AIRs. This work is embarrassingly parallel — each AIR's post-processing is independent. Restructuring the loop to collect raw GPU results first, then batch-process them with rayon's `par_iter` across 32 cores, should reduce this CPU overhead from ~200ms to ~7-13ms, yielding an estimated 28% improvement on Round 0 and 7-8% on STARK excl trace.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-12-2130-pipeline-round0-kernel-launches","+# 2026-04-12-2245-parallelize-round0-cpu-postprocess"," ","-The Round 0 constraint evaluation loop in `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` processes each AIR instance sequentially with two GPU sync points per AIR (`to_host()` at lines 792 and 848). With 623 AIR instances at APC 300, this creates 1,246 GPU synchronizations that serialize the pipeline and prevent the GPU from keeping its execution queue full. Eliminating these per-AIR sync points by deferring all D2H copies to after all kernel launches will allow the GPU to execute kernels back-to-back, reducing Round 0 from ~662ms to an estimated ~300-400ms at APC 300.","+Round 0 constraint evaluation at APC 300 spends ~200ms of its 662ms total on serial CPU post-processing (transpose + iDFT + polynomial construction), executed once per AIR × 3 calls inside a sequential loop over 623 AIRs. This work is embarrassingly parallel — each AIR's post-processing is independent. Restructuring the loop to collect raw GPU results first, then batch-process them with rayon's `par_iter` across 32 cores, should reduce this CPU overhead from ~200ms to ~7-13ms, yielding an estimated 28% improvement on Round 0 and 7-8% on STARK excl trace."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-12-2130-pipeline-round0-kernel-launches\n\nThe Round 0 constraint evaluation loop in `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` processes each AIR instance sequentially with two GPU sync points per AIR (`to_host()` at lines 792 and 848). With 623 AIR instances at APC 300, this creates 1,246 GPU synchronizations that serialize the pipeline and prevent the GPU from keeping its execution queue full. Eliminating these per-AIR sync points by deferring all D2H copies to after all kernel launches will allow the GPU to execute kernels back-to-back, reducing Round 0 from ~662ms to an estimated ~300-400ms at APC 300.\n"}}
