{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DqC2Bkr7MAyWryPm6zGLcC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-12-2245-parallelize-round0-cpu-postprocess\n2\t\n3\tRound 0 constraint evaluation at APC 300 spends ~200ms of its 662ms total on serial CPU post-processing (transpose + iDFT + polynomial construction), executed once per AIR × 3 calls inside a sequential loop over 623 AIRs. This work is embarrassingly parallel — each AIR's post-processing is independent. Restructuring the loop to collect raw GPU results first, then batch-process them with rayon's `par_iter` across 32 cores, should reduce this CPU overhead from ~200ms to ~7-13ms, yielding an estimated 28% improvement on Round 0 and 7-8% on STARK excl trace.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01H1fUV5RviQcwYMdp8S5p5A","session_id":"f1ad9314-c536-427a-92c1-585cbcf5d248","uuid":"c6234c38-e7d0-4093-a0e0-3f0979cd931b","timestamp":"2026-04-12T20:08:10.336Z"}
