{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018BAACxHuovhNYYWkdtpnD2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Parallelize Round 0 CPU Post-Processing\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce Round 0 time at APC 300 from ~662ms to ~475ms by parallelizing the CPU-bound post-processing (transpose + iDFT + polynomial construction) across AIRs using rayon. The current implementation processes 623 AIRs sequentially, spending ~200ms on CPU-only work that is embarrassingly parallel. With 32 cores, this drops to ~7-13ms.\n6\t\n7\tThis addresses the core scaling problem: as APC count increases, AIR count grows (99 → 623) but per-AIR work shrinks. The per-AIR CPU overhead becomes dominant, accounting for ~30% of Round 0 time at APC 300 vs ~3% at APC 0.\n8\t\n9\t## Current Code Path\n10\t\n11\t### Entry point\n12\t`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:598-884`\n13\t\n14\t### Pre-loop setup (lines 606-728)\n15\t- Lambda powers upload (line 610)\n16\t- Lambda combinations for AIRs with monomials (lines 617-624)\n17\t- eq_3b computation per trace (lines 628-671)\n18\t- Logup combinations per trace (lines 674-691)\n19\t- EqEvalLayers construction (lines 695-703)\n20\t- Selector matrices per trace (lines 705-718)\n21\t\n22\tThis section is unchanged by the optimization.\n23\t\n24\t### The per-AIR loop (lines 732-880) — THIS IS WHAT CHANGES\n25\t\n26\tFor each of 623 AIRs, the loop currently performs:\n27\t\n28\t**A. GPU constraint work (lines 744-790):**\n29\t1. Build `SymbolicConstraints` from proving key (line 744-745)\n30\t2. Compute `omega_root`, gather trace pointers (lines 757-768)\n31\t3. Call `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` → returns `sum_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>` (lines 777-790)\n32\t\n33\t**B. CPU constraint post-processing (lines 791-827):**\n34\t1. `sum_buffer.to_host()` — D2H sync point (line 792)\n35\t2. Transpose `q_evals` from coset-major to row-major (lines 795-801)\n36\t3. `UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft()` — serial CPU iDFT (lines 802-806)\n37\t4. Polynomial coefficient assembly via `(Z^{2^l_skip} - 1) * q` (lines 810-818)\n38\t5. Store into `batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + trace_idx]` (line 826)\n39\t\n40\t**C. GPU interaction work (lines 831-846):**\n41\t1. Call `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` which internally:\n42\t   - Builds symbolic DAG for interactions (round0.rs:162-180)\n43\t   - Compiles to `SymbolicRulesGpu`, computes weights (round0.rs:181-206)\n44\t   - Uploads rules + weights to GPU (round0.rs:204-210)\n45\t   - Launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` kernel (round0.rs:250-272)\n46\t   - Returns `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` (line 831)\n47\t\n48\t**D. CPU interaction post-processing (lines 847-879):**\n49\t1. `sum.to_host()` — D2H sync point (line 848)\n50\t2. Unzip fractions into numerator/denominator vectors (line 849-850)\n51\t3. Optional normalization for negative `n` (lines 851-857)\n52\t4. Transpose numer/denom from coset-major to row-major (lines 858-867)\n53\t5. `from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft()` × 2 — serial CPU iDFT for numer and denom (lines 869-878)\n54\t6. Store into `batch_sp_poly[2*trace_idx]` and `batch_sp_poly[2*trace_idx + 1]` (lines 869, 874)\n55\t\n56\t### Why it's slow\n57\t\n58\tSteps B and D are CPU-only and executed **sequentially** for 623 AIRs. Each includes:\n59\t- 1-2 transpose operations: O(num_cosets × 2^l_skip)\n60\t- 1-3 iDFT calls: O(degree × log(degree)) each (tiny per AIR but 1,869 calls total)\n61\t- Polynomial coefficient assembly\n62\t\n63\tTotal CPU post-processing: ~200ms (measured: 662ms total - 462ms GPU kernel time from nsight)\n64\t\n65\tThe GPU is idle during CPU post-processing. With 623 AIRs, that's ~0.32ms per AIR × 623 = 200ms of GPU-idle time.\n66\t\n67\t## Changes\n68\t\n69\t### Change 1: Add `rayon` dependency to cuda-backend\n70\t\n71\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/Cargo.toml`\n72\t\n73\tAdd `p3-maybe-rayon` as a dependency and add a `parallel` feature:\n74\t\n75\t```toml\n76\t[dependencies]\n77\t...\n78\tp3-maybe-rayon.workspace = true\n79\t\n80\t[features]\n81\tdefault = []\n82\tparallel = [\"p3-maybe-rayon/parallel\"]\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\t**Why:** Enables `par_iter()` when the `parallel` feature is active (which it is in production builds). Falls back to serial `iter()` without the feature.\n86\t\n87\t### Change 2: Define a struct for raw Round 0 per-AIR results\n88\t\n89\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n90\t\n91\tAdd a local struct (private, inside the impl block or at module level) to hold raw D2H data and the metadata needed for CPU post-processing:\n92\t\n93\t```rust\n94\t/// Raw per-AIR data collected during GPU phase of Round 0,\n95\t/// to be post-processed in parallel.\n96\tstruct Round0AirRaw {\n97\t    trace_idx: usize,\n98\t    n: i32,\n99\t    local_constraint_deg: usize,\n100\t    omega_root: F,\n101\t\n102\t    /// Raw D2H constraint evaluations, or None if no constraints\n103\t    constraint_evals: Option<Vec<EF>>,\n104\t    /// Raw D2H interaction evaluations, or None if no interactions\n105\t    interaction_evals: Option<Vec<Frac<EF>>>,\n106\t}\n107\t```\n108\t\n109\t**Why:** Decouples GPU result collection from CPU post-processing. Each instance is self-contained with all metadata needed for independent processing.\n110\t\n111\t### Change 3: Split the per-AIR loop into Phase 1 (GPU) and Phase 2 (CPU)\n112\t\n113\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`, lines 730-880\n114\t\n115\tReplace the single loop body with two phases:\n116\t\n117\t**Phase 1 — GPU work + D2H collection (sequential):**\n118\t\n119\tKeep the loop structure at lines 732-739. Inside the loop body:\n120\t- Keep lines 741-790 unchanged (constraint data prep + GPU kernel launch)\n121\t- At line 791-792: Do `to_host()` and store the raw `Vec<EF>` into `Round0AirRaw.constraint_evals` (but do NOT do the transpose/iDFT/polynomial construction)\n122\t- Keep lines 830-846 unchanged (interaction GPU kernel launch)\n123\t- At line 847-848: Do `to_host()` and store the raw `Vec<Frac<EF>>` into `Round0AirRaw.interaction_evals` (but do NOT do the transpose/iDFT/polynomial construction)\n124\t- Push the `Round0AirRaw` onto a `Vec<Round0AirRaw>`\n125\t\n126\tThis phase retains all GPU kernel launches and D2H copies in order. The only change is removing CPU post-processing from the loop body.\n127\t\n128\t**Phase 2 — CPU post-processing (parallel with rayon):**\n129\t\n130\tAfter the GPU loop completes:\n131\t\n132\t```rust\n133\tuse p3_maybe_rayon::prelude::*;\n134\t\n135\tlet results: Vec<(usize, Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>, Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>, Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>)> = \n136\t    raw_results.into_par_iter().map(|raw| {\n137\t        let l_skip = l_skip; // captured from outer scope\n138\t        let num_present_airs = num_present_airs;\n139\t        \n140\t        // Constraint post-processing (former lines 792-827)\n141\t        let zc_poly = raw.constraint_evals.map(|q_evals| {\n142\t            let num_cosets_zc = raw.local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n143\t            // Transpose\n144\t            let mut values = EF::zero_vec(num_cosets_zc << l_skip);\n145\t            for coset_idx in 0..num_cosets_zc {\n146\t                for i in 0..1 << l_skip {\n147\t                    values[i * num_cosets_zc + coset_idx] = q_evals[(coset_idx << l_skip) + i];\n148\t                }\n149\t            }\n150\t            let q = UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft(\n151\t                RowMajorMatrix::new(values, num_cosets_zc),\n152\t                raw.omega_root,\n153\t                raw.omega_root,\n154\t            );\n155\t            // sp_0 = (Z^{2^l_skip} - 1) * q\n156\t            let sp_0_deg = sumcheck_round0_deg(l_skip, raw.local_constraint_deg);\n157\t            let coeffs = (0..=sp_0_deg)\n158\t                .map(|i| {\n159\t                    let mut c = -*q.coeffs().get(i).unwrap_or(&EF::ZERO);\n160\t                    if i >= 1 << l_skip { c += q.coeffs()[i - (1 << l_skip)]; }\n161\t                    c\n162\t                })\n163\t                .collect_vec();\n164\t            UnivariatePoly::new(coeffs)\n165\t        });\n166\t        \n167\t        // Interaction post-processing (former lines 847-879)\n168\t        let (numer_poly, denom_poly) = if let Some(evals) = raw.interaction_evals {\n169\t            let num_cosets_logup = raw.local_constraint_deg;\n170\t            let (mut numer, denom): (Vec<EF>, Vec<EF>) =\n171\t                evals.into_iter().map(|frac| (frac.p, frac.q)).unzip();\n172\t            if raw.n < 0 {\n173\t                let norm_factor = F::from_u32(1 << (-raw.n) as u32).inverse();\n174\t                for s in &mut numer { *s *= norm_factor; }\n175\t            }\n176\t            let mut numer_values = EF::zero_vec(num_cosets_logup << l_skip);\n177\t            let mut denom_values = EF::zero_vec(num_cosets_logup << l_skip);\n178\t            for coset_idx in 0..num_cosets_logup {\n179\t                for i in 0..1 << l_skip {\n180\t                    let src = (coset_idx << l_skip) + i;\n181\t                    let dst = i * num_cosets_logup + coset_idx;\n182\t                    numer_values[dst] = numer[src];\n183\t                    denom_values[dst] = denom[src];\n184\t                }\n185\t            }\n186\t            let np = UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft(\n187\t                RowMajorMatrix::new(numer_values, num_cosets_logup),\n188\t                raw.omega_root, F::ONE,\n189\t            );\n190\t            let dp = UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft(\n191\t                RowMajorMatrix::new(denom_values, num_cosets_logup),\n192\t                raw.omega_root, F::ONE,\n193\t            );\n194\t            (Some(np), Some(dp))\n195\t        } else {\n196\t            (None, None)\n197\t        };\n198\t        \n199\t        (raw.trace_idx, numer_poly, denom_poly, zc_poly)\n200\t    }).collect();\n201\t\n202\t// Scatter results into batch_sp_poly\n203\tfor (trace_idx, numer_poly, denom_poly, zc_poly) in results {\n204\t    if let Some(p) = numer_poly {\n205\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx] = p;\n206\t    }\n207\t    if let Some(p) = denom_poly {\n208\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx + 1] = p;\n209\t    }\n210\t    if let Some(p) = zc_poly {\n211\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + trace_idx] = p;\n212\t    }\n213\t}\n214\t```\n215\t\n216\t**Why this is the critical change:** The `from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft` calls (3 per AIR × 623 AIRs = 1,869 calls) and the transpose operations are the CPU bottleneck. By moving them to `par_iter`, they execute across all 32 cores simultaneously. Expected speedup: 200ms / 32 ≈ 7ms (theoretical), ~13ms (realistic with rayon overhead).\n217\t\n218\t### Change 4: Retain the debug_assert for zerocheck sum\n219\t\n220\tThe `debug_assert_eq!` at line 819-824 that checks the zerocheck sum is zero should be preserved inside the parallel closure. It accesses `ctx.per_trace[trace_idx].0` which we need to capture. Include `air_idx` in `Round0AirRaw`:\n221\t\n222\t```rust\n223\tstruct Round0AirRaw {\n224\t    trace_idx: usize,\n225\t    air_idx: usize,  // for debug_assert\n226\t    n: i32,\n227\t    ...\n228\t}\n229\t```\n230\t\n231\t### Change 5: Feature-gate parallel import\n232\t\n233\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n234\t\n235\tAdd at the top of the file:\n236\t```rust\n237\tuse p3_maybe_rayon::prelude::*;\n238\t```\n239\t\n240\tThis import provides `par_iter()` when `parallel` is enabled and falls back to `iter()` when it's not.\n241\t\n242\t## Invariants\n243\t\n244\t1. **Output equivalence:** `batch_sp_poly` must contain exactly the same polynomials in the same positions as the current code. Each element is computed from the same raw data using the same arithmetic.\n245\t\n246\t2. **GPU kernel ordering:** All GPU kernels are still launched in the same order on the same CUDA stream. Phase 1 does not change GPU behavior.\n247\t\n248\t3. **D2H sync correctness:** Each `to_host()` call still synchronizes the stream before returning data. The data is fully materialized before being stored in `Round0AirRaw`.\n249\t\n250\t4. **No CUDA calls from rayon threads:** Phase 2 is pure CPU. No `DeviceBuffer`, `to_device()`, or CUDA FFI calls occur inside `par_iter`. This avoids CUDA context issues with rayon worker threads.\n251\t\n252\t5. **Memory safety:** `Round0AirRaw` owns its `Vec<EF>` and `Vec<Frac<EF>>` data. No references to `DeviceBuffer` or GPU memory. All GPU buffers are dropped at the end of Phase 1.\n253\t\n254\t6. **Deterministic output:** The polynomial operations (transpose, iDFT, coefficient assembly) are deterministic. Parallel execution does not change results because each AIR is processed independently and results are scattered by index.\n255\t\n256\t## Measurement Plan\n257\t\n258\t### Commands\n259\t\n260\tRun in the powdr repo:\n261\t```bash\n262\topenvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh\n263\t```\n264\t\n265\tFor each APC config {0, 100, 300}, analyze with:\n266\t```bash\n267\tpython spec.py <metrics_json_path> <experiment_name>\n268\t```\n269\t\n270\t### Expected results\n271\t\n272\t| Metric | Baseline (APC 300) | Expected After | Change |\n273\t|--------|-------------------|----------------|--------|\n274\t| Round 0 | 662ms | 462-490ms | -172 to -200ms (-26 to -30%) |\n275\t| STARK excl trace | 2464ms | 2264-2300ms | -164 to -200ms (-7 to -8%) |\n276\t| Round 0 (APC 0) | 177ms | 170-177ms | ~0ms (few AIRs, low parallel benefit) |\n277\t\n278\tThe improvement should be proportional to AIR count:\n279\t- APC 0 (99 AIRs): minimal improvement (CPU overhead is small)\n280\t- APC 100 (360 AIRs): moderate improvement  \n281\t- APC 300 (623 AIRs): largest improvement\n282\t\n283\t### Verification\n284\t\n285\t1. The prove+verify cycle must succeed for all three APC configs\n286\t2. No correctness regressions (proofs must verify)\n287\t3. No memory regressions (check `nvidia-smi` peak GPU memory)\n288\t\n289\t## Rollback Criteria\n290\t\n291\t- **Less than 10% improvement** in Round 0 at APC 300 (< 66ms reduction): ROLLBACK\n292\t- Correctness failure (proof doesn't verify): ROLLBACK immediately\n293\t- APC 0 regression > 5% on STARK excl trace: ROLLBACK\n294\t- GPU memory peak increases by > 10%: ROLLBACK\n295\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01H1fUV5RviQcwYMdp8S5p5A","session_id":"f1ad9314-c536-427a-92c1-585cbcf5d248","uuid":"208c5d2a-97d1-4666-9bc4-a7da91b25abc","timestamp":"2026-04-12T20:08:11.143Z"}
