{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_017UxD88gTtiyAr5fzZcz1vt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0151cUyLFLRyPgQB1rr6ihPd","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-12-2245-parallelize-round0-cpu-postprocess/plan.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1642,"cache_read_input_tokens":7501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1642,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WjQzKcf5YBN8o2NmC1Vhua","session_id":"f1ad9314-c536-427a-92c1-585cbcf5d248","uuid":"1c11374e-4ce5-45bb-bdf4-e9810fe28898"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0151cUyLFLRyPgQB1rr6ihPd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Parallelize Round 0 CPU Post-Processing\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce Round 0 time at APC 300 from ~662ms to ~475ms by parallelizing the CPU-bound post-processing (transpose + iDFT + polynomial construction) across AIRs using rayon. The current implementation processes 623 AIRs sequentially, spending ~200ms on CPU-only work that is embarrassingly parallel. With 32 cores, this drops to ~7-13ms.\n6\t\n7\tThis addresses the core scaling problem: as APC count increases, AIR count grows (99 → 623) but per-AIR work shrinks. The per-AIR CPU overhead becomes dominant, accounting for ~30% of Round 0 time at APC 300 vs ~3% at APC 0.\n8\t\n9\t## Current Code Path\n10\t\n11\t### Entry point\n12\t`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:598-884`\n13\t\n14\t### Pre-loop setup (lines 606-728)\n15\t- Lambda powers upload (line 610)\n16\t- Lambda combinations for AIRs with monomials (lines 617-624)\n17\t- eq_3b computation per trace (lines 628-671)\n18\t- Logup combinations per trace (lines 674-691)\n19\t- EqEvalLayers construction (lines 695-703)\n20\t- Selector matrices per trace (lines 705-718)\n21\t\n22\tThis section is unchanged by the optimization.\n23\t\n24\t### The per-AIR loop (lines 732-880) — THIS IS WHAT CHANGES\n25\t\n26\tFor each of 623 AIRs, the loop currently performs:\n27\t\n28\t**A. GPU constraint work (lines 744-790):**\n29\t1. Build `SymbolicConstraints` from proving key (line 744-745)\n30\t2. Compute `omega_root`, gather trace pointers (lines 757-768)\n31\t3. Call `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` → returns `sum_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>` (lines 777-790)\n32\t\n33\t**B. CPU constraint post-processing (lines 791-827):**\n34\t1. `sum_buffer.to_host()` — D2H sync point (line 792)\n35\t2. Transpose `q_evals` from coset-major to row-major (lines 795-801)\n36\t3. `UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft()` — serial CPU iDFT (lines 802-806)\n37\t4. Polynomial coefficient assembly via `(Z^{2^l_skip} - 1) * q` (lines 810-818)\n38\t5. Store into `batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + trace_idx]` (line 826)\n39\t\n40\t**C. GPU interaction work (lines 831-846):**\n41\t1. Call `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` which internally:\n42\t   - Builds symbolic DAG for interactions (round0.rs:162-180)\n43\t   - Compiles to `SymbolicRulesGpu`, computes weights (round0.rs:181-206)\n44\t   - Uploads rules + weights to GPU (round0.rs:204-210)\n45\t   - Launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` kernel (round0.rs:250-272)\n46\t   - Returns `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` (line 831)\n47\t\n48\t**D. CPU interaction post-processing (lines 847-879):**\n49\t1. `sum.to_host()` — D2H sync point (line 848)\n50\t2. Unzip fractions into numerator/denominator vectors (line 849-850)\n51\t3. Optional normalization for negative `n` (lines 851-857)\n52\t4. Transpose numer/denom from coset-major to row-major (lines 858-867)\n53\t5. `from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft()` × 2 — serial CPU iDFT for numer and denom (lines 869-878)\n54\t6. Store into `batch_sp_poly[2*trace_idx]` and `batch_sp_poly[2*trace_idx + 1]` (lines 869, 874)\n55\t\n56\t### Why it's slow\n57\t\n58\tSteps B and D are CPU-only and executed **sequentially** for 623 AIRs. Each includes:\n59\t- 1-2 transpose operations: O(num_cosets × 2^l_skip)\n60\t- 1-3 iDFT calls: O(degree × log(degree)) each (tiny per AIR but 1,869 calls total)\n61\t- Polynomial coefficient assembly\n62\t\n63\tTotal CPU post-processing: ~200ms (measured: 662ms total - 462ms GPU kernel time from nsight)\n64\t\n65\tThe GPU is idle during CPU post-processing. With 623 AIRs, that's ~0.32ms per AIR × 623 = 200ms of GPU-idle time.\n66\t\n67\t## Changes\n68\t\n69\t### Change 1: No new dependency needed — use existing re-export\n70\t\n71\t**File:** No Cargo.toml changes required.\n72\t\n73\t`openvm-stark-backend` already re-exports `p3_maybe_rayon` at `crates/stark-backend/src/lib.rs:12`, and its `parallel` feature is already enabled by the powdr workspace. Due to Cargo feature unification, `p3_maybe_rayon` with rayon support is already active in the cuda-backend's dependency tree.\n74\t\n75\tNo new dependency or feature flag is needed. The cuda-backend accesses rayon via:\n76\t```rust\n77\tuse openvm_stark_backend::p3_maybe_rayon::prelude::*;\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\t**Why:** Adding a separate `parallel` feature to cuda-backend would require downstream consumers (powdr, openvm) to explicitly enable it. Currently none of them do, so `par_iter()` would silently fall back to serial `iter()`, making the optimization a no-op. Using the existing re-export avoids this entirely.\n81\t\n82\t### Change 2: Define a struct for raw Round 0 per-AIR results\n83\t\n84\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n85\t\n86\tAdd a local struct (private, inside the impl block or at module level) to hold raw D2H data and the metadata needed for CPU post-processing:\n87\t\n88\t```rust\n89\t/// Raw per-AIR data collected during GPU phase of Round 0,\n90\t/// to be post-processed in parallel.\n91\tstruct Round0AirRaw {\n92\t    trace_idx: usize,\n93\t    n: i32,\n94\t    local_constraint_deg: usize,\n95\t    omega_root: F,\n96\t\n97\t    /// Raw D2H constraint evaluations, or None if no constraints\n98\t    constraint_evals: Option<Vec<EF>>,\n99\t    /// Raw D2H interaction evaluations, or None if no interactions\n100\t    interaction_evals: Option<Vec<Frac<EF>>>,\n101\t}\n102\t```\n103\t\n104\t**Why:** Decouples GPU result collection from CPU post-processing. Each instance is self-contained with all metadata needed for independent processing.\n105\t\n106\t### Change 3: Split the per-AIR loop into Phase 1 (GPU) and Phase 2 (CPU)\n107\t\n108\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`, lines 730-880\n109\t\n110\tReplace the single loop body with two phases:\n111\t\n112\t**Phase 1 — GPU work + D2H collection (sequential):**\n113\t\n114\tKeep the loop structure at lines 732-739. Inside the loop body:\n115\t- Keep lines 741-790 unchanged (constraint data prep + GPU kernel launch)\n116\t- At line 791-792: Do `to_host()` and store the raw `Vec<EF>` into `Round0AirRaw.constraint_evals` (but do NOT do the transpose/iDFT/polynomial construction)\n117\t- Keep lines 830-846 unchanged (interaction GPU kernel launch)\n118\t- At line 847-848: Do `to_host()` and store the raw `Vec<Frac<EF>>` into `Round0AirRaw.interaction_evals` (but do NOT do the transpose/iDFT/polynomial construction)\n119\t- Push the `Round0AirRaw` onto a `Vec<Round0AirRaw>`\n120\t\n121\tThis phase retains all GPU kernel launches and D2H copies in order. The only change is removing CPU post-processing from the loop body.\n122\t\n123\t**Phase 2 — CPU post-processing (parallel with rayon):**\n124\t\n125\tAfter the GPU loop completes:\n126\t\n127\t```rust\n128\t// p3_maybe_rayon imported at file top via openvm_stark_backend::p3_maybe_rayon::prelude::*\n129\t\n130\tlet results: Vec<(usize, Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>, Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>, Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>)> = \n131\t    raw_results.into_par_iter().map(|raw| {\n132\t        let l_skip = l_skip; // captured from outer scope\n133\t        let num_present_airs = num_present_airs;\n134\t        \n135\t        // Constraint post-processing (former lines 792-827)\n136\t        let zc_poly = raw.constraint_evals.map(|q_evals| {\n137\t            let num_cosets_zc = raw.local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n138\t            // Transpose\n139\t            let mut values = EF::zero_vec(num_cosets_zc << l_skip);\n140\t            for coset_idx in 0..num_cosets_zc {\n141\t                for i in 0..1 << l_skip {\n142\t                    values[i * num_cosets_zc + coset_idx] = q_evals[(coset_idx << l_skip) + i];\n143\t                }\n144\t            }\n145\t            let q = UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft(\n146\t                RowMajorMatrix::new(values, num_cosets_zc),\n147\t                raw.omega_root,\n148\t                raw.omega_root,\n149\t            );\n150\t            // sp_0 = (Z^{2^l_skip} - 1) * q\n151\t            let sp_0_deg = sumcheck_round0_deg(l_skip, raw.local_constraint_deg);\n152\t            let coeffs = (0..=sp_0_deg)\n153\t                .map(|i| {\n154\t                    let mut c = -*q.coeffs().get(i).unwrap_or(&EF::ZERO);\n155\t                    if i >= 1 << l_skip { c += q.coeffs()[i - (1 << l_skip)]; }\n156\t                    c\n157\t                })\n158\t                .collect_vec();\n159\t            UnivariatePoly::new(coeffs)\n160\t        });\n161\t        \n162\t        // Interaction post-processing (former lines 847-879)\n163\t        let (numer_poly, denom_poly) = if let Some(evals) = raw.interaction_evals {\n164\t            let num_cosets_logup = raw.local_constraint_deg;\n165\t            let (mut numer, denom): (Vec<EF>, Vec<EF>) =\n166\t                evals.into_iter().map(|frac| (frac.p, frac.q)).unzip();\n167\t            if raw.n.is_negative() {\n168\t                let norm_factor = F::from_u32(1 << raw.n.unsigned_abs()).inverse();\n169\t                for s in &mut numer { *s *= norm_factor; }\n170\t            }\n171\t            let mut numer_values = EF::zero_vec(num_cosets_logup << l_skip);\n172\t            let mut denom_values = EF::zero_vec(num_cosets_logup << l_skip);\n173\t            for coset_idx in 0..num_cosets_logup {\n174\t                for i in 0..1 << l_skip {\n175\t                    let src = (coset_idx << l_skip) + i;\n176\t                    let dst = i * num_cosets_logup + coset_idx;\n177\t                    numer_values[dst] = numer[src];\n178\t                    denom_values[dst] = denom[src];\n179\t                }\n180\t            }\n181\t            let np = UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft(\n182\t                RowMajorMatrix::new(numer_values, num_cosets_logup),\n183\t                raw.omega_root, F::ONE,\n184\t            );\n185\t            let dp = UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft(\n186\t                RowMajorMatrix::new(denom_values, num_cosets_logup),\n187\t                raw.omega_root, F::ONE,\n188\t            );\n189\t            (Some(np), Some(dp))\n190\t        } else {\n191\t            (None, None)\n192\t        };\n193\t        \n194\t        (raw.trace_idx, numer_poly, denom_poly, zc_poly)\n195\t    }).collect();\n196\t\n197\t// Scatter results into batch_sp_poly\n198\tfor (trace_idx, numer_poly, denom_poly, zc_poly) in results {\n199\t    if let Some(p) = numer_poly {\n200\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx] = p;\n201\t    }\n202\t    if let Some(p) = denom_poly {\n203\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx + 1] = p;\n204\t    }\n205\t    if let Some(p) = zc_poly {\n206\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + trace_idx] = p;\n207\t    }\n208\t}\n209\t```\n210\t\n211\t**Why this is the critical change:** The `from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft` calls (3 per AIR × 623 AIRs = 1,869 calls) and the transpose operations are the CPU bottleneck. By moving them to `par_iter`, they execute across all 32 cores simultaneously. Expected speedup: 200ms / 32 ≈ 7ms (theoretical), ~13ms (realistic with rayon overhead).\n212\t\n213\t### Change 4: Retain the debug_assert for zerocheck sum\n214\t\n215\tThe `debug_assert_eq!` at line 819-824 that checks the zerocheck sum is zero must be preserved inside the parallel closure. It accesses `ctx.per_trace[trace_idx].0` which is the `air_idx`. Include `air_idx` in `Round0AirRaw`:\n216\t\n217\t```rust\n218\tstruct Round0AirRaw {\n219\t    trace_idx: usize,\n220\t    air_idx: usize,  // for debug_assert in zerocheck sum check\n221\t    n: i32,\n222\t    ...\n223\t}\n224\t```\n225\t\n226\tInside the constraint post-processing closure (after computing `coeffs`), add:\n227\t```rust\n228\tdebug_assert_eq!(\n229\t    coeffs.iter().step_by(1 << l_skip).copied().sum::<EF>(),\n230\t    EF::ZERO,\n231\t    \"Zerocheck sum is not zero for air_id: {}\",\n232\t    raw.air_idx\n233\t);\n234\t```\n235\t\n236\t### Change 5: Add import for rayon prelude\n237\t\n238\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n239\t\n240\tAdd at the top of the file:\n241\t```rust\n242\tuse openvm_stark_backend::p3_maybe_rayon::prelude::*;\n243\t```\n244\t\n245\tThis import provides `par_iter()` / `into_par_iter()` when the `parallel` feature is active (which it already is through the stark-backend dependency chain). Without `parallel`, it falls back to serial `iter()` / `into_iter()`.\n246\t\n247\t## Invariants\n248\t\n249\t1. **Output equivalence:** `batch_sp_poly` must contain exactly the same polynomials in the same positions as the current code. Each element is computed from the same raw data using the same arithmetic.\n250\t\n251\t2. **GPU kernel ordering:** All GPU kernels are still launched in the same order on the same CUDA stream. Phase 1 does not change GPU behavior.\n252\t\n253\t3. **D2H sync correctness:** Each `to_host()` call still synchronizes the stream before returning data. The data is fully materialized before being stored in `Round0AirRaw`.\n254\t\n255\t4. **No CUDA calls from rayon threads:** Phase 2 is pure CPU. No `DeviceBuffer`, `to_device()`, or CUDA FFI calls occur inside `par_iter`. This avoids CUDA context issues with rayon worker threads.\n256\t\n257\t5. **Memory safety:** `Round0AirRaw` owns its `Vec<EF>` and `Vec<Frac<EF>>` data. No references to `DeviceBuffer` or GPU memory. All GPU buffers are dropped at the end of Phase 1.\n258\t\n259\t6. **Deterministic output:** The polynomial operations (transpose, iDFT, coefficient assembly) are deterministic. Parallel execution does not change results because each AIR is processed independently and results are scattered by index.\n260\t\n261\t## Measurement Plan\n262\t\n263\t### Commands\n264\t\n265\tRun in the powdr repo:\n266\t```bash\n267\topenvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh\n268\t```\n269\t\n270\tFor each APC config {0, 100, 300}, analyze with:\n271\t```bash\n272\tpython spec.py <metrics_json_path> <experiment_name>\n273\t```\n274\t\n275\t### Expected results\n276\t\n277\t| Metric | Baseline (APC 300) | Expected After | Change |\n278\t|--------|-------------------|----------------|--------|\n279\t| Round 0 | 662ms | 462-490ms | -172 to -200ms (-26 to -30%) |\n280\t| STARK excl trace | 2464ms | 2264-2300ms | -164 to -200ms (-7 to -8%) |\n281\t| Round 0 (APC 0) | 177ms | 170-177ms | ~0ms (few AIRs, low parallel benefit) |\n282\t\n283\tThe improvement should be proportional to AIR count:\n284\t- APC 0 (99 AIRs): minimal improvement (CPU overhead is small)\n285\t- APC 100 (360 AIRs): moderate improvement  \n286\t- APC 300 (623 AIRs): largest improvement\n287\t\n288\t### Verification\n289\t\n290\t1. The prove+verify cycle must succeed for all three APC configs\n291\t2. No correctness regressions (proofs must verify)\n292\t3. No memory regressions (check `nvidia-smi` peak GPU memory)\n293\t\n294\t## Rollback Criteria\n295\t\n296\t- **Less than 10% improvement** in Round 0 at APC 300 (< 66ms reduction): ROLLBACK\n297\t- Correctness failure (proof doesn't verify): ROLLBACK immediately\n298\t- APC 0 regression > 5% on STARK excl trace: ROLLBACK\n299\t- GPU memory peak increases by > 10%: ROLLBACK\n300\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WjQzKcf5YBN8o2NmC1Vhua","session_id":"f1ad9314-c536-427a-92c1-585cbcf5d248","uuid":"e99b8640-3a4e-428b-a2b5-d6e0fb0364ee","timestamp":"2026-04-12T20:11:07.182Z"}
