{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KrDxaXtEewYMWyfYzH2AXP","type":"tool_result","content":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-12-2245-parallelize-round0-cpu-postprocess\n\nRound 0 constraint evaluation at APC 300 spends ~200ms of its 662ms total on serial CPU post-processing (transpose + iDFT + polynomial construction), executed once per AIR × 3 calls inside a sequential loop over 623 AIRs. This work is embarrassingly parallel — each AIR's post-processing is independent. Restructuring the loop to collect raw GPU results first, then batch-process them with rayon's `par_iter` across 32 cores, should reduce this CPU overhead from ~200ms to ~7-13ms, yielding an estimated 28% improvement on Round 0 and 7-8% on STARK excl trace.\n\n=== plan.md ===\n# Plan: Parallelize Round 0 CPU Post-Processing\n\n## Goal\n\n=== baseline/ ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\nnsys_apc300.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc300.sqlite\nsummary.md\n\n=== log.md ===\n## 2026-04-12-2130-pipeline-round0-kernel-launches\n\n**Idea**: Eliminate per-AIR GPU synchronization in Round 0 by restructuring the loop into prepare/launch/collect phases.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1ad9314-c536-427a-92c1-585cbcf5d248","uuid":"27f4f48a-39f4-44bc-b27b-6e1be985d579","timestamp":"2026-04-12T20:14:13.951Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-12-2245-parallelize-round0-cpu-postprocess\n\nRound 0 constraint evaluation at APC 300 spends ~200ms of its 662ms total on serial CPU post-processing (transpose + iDFT + polynomial construction), executed once per AIR × 3 calls inside a sequential loop over 623 AIRs. This work is embarrassingly parallel — each AIR's post-processing is independent. Restructuring the loop to collect raw GPU results first, then batch-process them with rayon's `par_iter` across 32 cores, should reduce this CPU overhead from ~200ms to ~7-13ms, yielding an estimated 28% improvement 